\par }{\b\fs28\cf2\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Workings of the Arith2 module
\par }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par Arith2 is a module of activity automation written for the Clic programme. Its function is to create the content files that Clic will use in the mental arithmeti
c activities. In these content files, arithmetical operations randomly generated according to the parameters indicated in the }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 configuration dialogue}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 CONFIGURE}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  are written.
\par }\pard\plain \s16\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
The conditions that must be adjusted in order to generate the activities are:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-3261\li3261\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx3261\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin3261\itap0 {\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Type of operations:}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  \tab You can choose from the }{
\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 operations}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_OPER}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  add, subtraction, multiplication and division, or any combination of them.
\par 
\par }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Expressions:}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  \tab The }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 unknown}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_INCOG}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 may be either one of the two operators, the result or even the operator. The operations can also be written backwards (C=A@B instead of A@B=C).
\par 
\par }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Limits of the operators:}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  \tab To }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 limit}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_LIMOP}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 the group of possible operators you can choose between setting a higher limit and a lower one, or writing a closed list of values. Optionally, you can also determine the appearance of the numbers 0, 1 and -1.
\par 
\par }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Number of decimals:}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  \tab Arith2 can generate operations with integer or rational numbers with a precision in }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 decimals}{
\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_DECIMALS}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  of up to hundredths.
\par 
\par }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Conditions of the operators:}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  \tab Optionally you can choose one operator to be }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 bigger than the other}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_CONDI}
{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 .
\par 
\par }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Conditions of the result:}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  \tab The result can also be tailored to some }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 limits}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_LIMRES}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . The number of decimals of the result is determined by the decimals of the operators. Once the group of operations has been generated, the programme can }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 order}{
\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_ORDRE}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 them in the content files. This option is especially useful for creating puzzles and identification activities. In the addition and subtraction of integer numbers you can activate the }{\ul\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 "do not carry"}{
\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 TOPIC_NOPORT}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  option.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \page }{\cs17\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain 
